{{also|te-ar}}
==English==

===Etymology 1===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*der-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|teren}}, from {{inh|en|ang|teran||to tear, lacerate}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*teraną||to tear, tear apart, rip}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*der-||to tear, tear apart}}.

Cognate with {{cog|sco|tere}}, {{m|sco|teir}}, {{m|sco|tair||to rend, lacerate, wound, rip, tear out}}, {{cog|nl|teren||to eliminate, efface, live, survive by consumption}}, {{cog|de|zehren||to consume, misuse}}, {{cog|de|zerren||to tug, rip, tear}}, {{cog|da|tære||to consume}}, {{cog|sv|tära||to fret, consume, deplete, use up}}, {{cog|is|tæra||to clear, corrode}}. Outside Germanic, cognate to {{cog|grc|δέρω||to skin}}, {{cog|sq|ther||to slay, skin, pierce}}. {{doublet|en|tire}}.

