#* {{RQ:Allingham China Governess|chapter=6|passage='{{...}} I remember a lady coming to inspect St. Mary's Home where I was brought up and seeing us all in our lovely Elizabethan uniforms we were so proud of, and bursting into '''tears''' all over us because "it was wicked to dress us like charity children".{{nb...}}'}}
